Hyphenation data in this directory
==================================

One file, and it is not a pattern set. karyll reads its pattern sets from the
Kindle, at `/usr/java/lib/dictionaries/hyphen/` — see `crate::hyphen` — so
nothing here is a dictionary and none is bundled.


en.curation — break decisions for American English
--------------------------------------------------

From bokai, `src/text/hyphenation/dic/en.curation`, verbatim.

Break decisions taken by hand over the stock `hyph_en_US.dic` patterns, which
are generated from a word list by machine and are judged on aggregate. The
commonest few hundred words of English are on every page, so a division that
reads poorly in one of them is seen constantly, and no adjustment of the
pattern machinery reaches it — the decision is per word. The file states the
two rules it was produced by in its own header.

The patterns it decides over are the Kindle's own, read at run time from
`/usr/java/lib/dictionaries/hyphen/hyph_en_US.dic`.
